-<main id="main"><div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/buyers/">Buyers</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">New Construction</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Buying a new build on the Grand Strand</p><h1 class="detail-h1">New construction in Myrtle Beach:<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">what the price on the sign leaves out.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge, 30+ years on the Grand Strand &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 1, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">New construction here costs about what a nearly new house does. The sign leaves out three things: the full tax bill, the options and the deposits.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A new house here lists for about the same price per square foot as a house built 2016 to 2023 of similar size nearby. Most are being built inland, in large communities near Highway 90, Highway 22 and the Carolina Bays Parkway.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">What the sign leaves out is the full tax bill. For about 4 in 5 of the 2026 builder sales, the county still taxes only the lot. On a typical home you live in outside city limits, the yearly county bill goes from about $290 to about $1,210 once the county values the house.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Touring model homes? Bring your own agent to the first visit.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Set up my builder tour</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#new-or-nearly-new" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">New or nearly new</a></li><li><a href="#where" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Where</a></li><li><a href="#cost" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Cost</a></li><li><a href="#tax-bill" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What the price leaves out</a></li><li><a href="#your-agent" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Your own agent</a></li><li><a href="#incentives" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Incentives and lenders</a></li><li><a href="#how-long" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">How long it takes</a></li><li><a href="#inspections" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--