play:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;column-gap:2.2rem}}main#main h1{text-wrap:balance}main#main .c3-gchart{max-width:760px;box-sizing:border-box}@media (max-width:360px){main#main a.btn{white-space:nowrap;padding-left:1rem!important;padding-right:1rem!important}}@media (max-width:360px){main#main .c3-glance span.t{font-size:.92rem;line-height:1.25}}.c3-nc-ax{margin-bottom:.9rem}main#main #tax-bill table th:first-child{width:44%}</style><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The price per square foot will not decide it for you. Next to a house built 2016 to 2023 of similar size within a mile, about half of new houses list for less per square foot and half for more. Town by town, the typical prices are close too.</p><figure class="c3-nc-fig" role="group" aria-label="Typical asking price per square foot of new houses and of houses built 2016 to 2023, by town in Horry County"><span class="c3-nc-cap">Typical asking price per square foot, houses for sale</span><div class="c3-nc-key" aria-hidden="true"><span><i style="background:#c4783a"></i>New</span><span><i style="background:#5c6b78"></i>Nearly new: built 2016 to 2023</span></div><div class="c3-nc-town"><span class="tn">Conway</span><div class="c3-nc-row"><span>New</span><span class="bar"><i style="width:55.7%;background:#c4783a"></i></span><em>$182</em></div><div class="c3-nc-row"><span>Nearly new</span><span class="bar"><i style="width:59.6%;background:#5c6b78"></i></span><em>$195</em></div></div><div class="c3-nc-town"><span class="tn">Longs</span><div class="c3-nc-row"><span>New</span><span class="bar"><i style="width:57.7%;background:#c4783a"></i></span><em>$188</em></div><div class="c3-nc-row"><span>Nearly new</span><span class="bar"><i style="width:57.0%;background:#5c6b78"></i></span><em>$186</em></div></div><div class="c3-nc-town"><span class="tn">Myrtle Beach</span><div class="c3-nc-row"><span>New</span><span class="bar"><i style="width:72.1%;background:#c4783a"></i></span><em>$235</em></div><div class="c3-nc-row"><span>Nearly new</span><span class="bar"><i style="width:71.8%;background:#5c6b78"></i></span><em>$235</em></div></div><div class="c3-nc-town"><span class="tn">Little River</span><div class="c3-nc-row"><span>New</span><span class="bar"><i style="width:70.2%;background:#c4783a"></i></span><em>$229</em></div><div class="c3-nc-row"><span>Nearly new</span><span class="bar"><i style="width:67.9%;background:#5c6b78"></i></span><em>$222</em></div></div><div class="c3-nc-town"><span class="tn">Galivants Ferry</span><div class="c3-nc-row"><span>New</span><span class="bar"><i style="width:70.3%;background:#c4783a"></i></span><em>$230</em></div><div class="c3-nc-row"><span>Nearly new</span><span class="bar"><i style="width:67.0%;background:#5c6b78"></i></span><em>$219</em></div></div><div class="c3-nc-town"><span class="tn">North Myrtle Beach</span><div class="c3-nc-row"><span>New</span><span class="bar"><i style="width:100.0%;background:#c4783a"></i></span><em>$327</em></div><div class="c3-nc-row"><span>Nearly new</span><span class="bar"><i style="width:97.7%;background:#5c6b78"></i></span><em>$319</em></div></div><figcaption style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.55;margin:.8rem 0 0;padding:0">Houses for sale in Horry County, grouped by the town in the address. A Myrtle Beach address includes inland Carolina Forest. Typical means half are higher and half lower. Towns with at least 15 of each kind.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The lot is about the same size too. In Conway, Longs and Myrtle Beach addresses, a new house has about the same size lot as a house built 2016 to 2023 in the same town.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What does a new house give you?</h3><ul class="c3-nc-check" role="list" aria-label="What a new house gives you"><li><span><strong>No one has lived in it.</strong> If the builder has not started it, you also pick the plan and the finishes.</span></li><li><span><strong>A written warranty from the builder.</strong> The <a href="#warranty-law" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">warranty section</a> below lists what it covers.</span></li><li><span><strong>Built to today's codes.</strong> State law has the county or city <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t06c009.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">enforce the building codes</a>: building, electrical, plumbing, gas, energy and fire. East of U.S.&nbsp;17, state law also has insurers <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t38c073.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">count the building code</a>, the construction and roof tie-downs when they price wind coverage.</span></li><li><span><strong>Less flood risk, on average.</strong> About 1 in 20 new houses for sale is in a high-risk flood zone on the map of the Federal Emergency Management Agency (FEMA). Of all houses for sale, about 8 in 100 are. Our <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">coastal insurance guide</a> covers wind and flood coverage.</span></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Pick by your plans:</p><ul class="c3-nc-dec" role="list" aria-label="Which kind of house fits your plans"><li><span class="c3-nc-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10.8 12.2 20 3M16.8 6.2l2.5 2.5M14.3 8.7l2 2"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="15.5" r="4.5"/></svg></span><span class="k">You want to move in within a month</span><span class="d">Look at nearly new resales and at new houses that are finished and never lived in.</span></li><li><span class="c3-nc-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 5h16a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM3 10h18M8 3v4M16 3v4M8 14h.01M12 14h.01M16 14h.01M8 17.5h.01M12 17.5h.01"/></svg></span><span class="k">You want to pick the plan and the finishes</span><span class="d">Choose a house the builder has not started. Plan on about 6 months of building, more on your own lot.</span></li><li><span class="c3-nc-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 9.4c-.4-1-1.5-1.8-3-1.8-1.8 0-3 1-3 2.2 0 3 6 1.6 6 4.4 0 1.3-1.3 2.2-3 2.2-1.6 0-2.7-.7-3.1-1.8M12 5.8v1.8M12 16.4v1.8"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/></svg></span><span class="k">You are buying it to rent</span><span class="d">The county taxes a rental or second home on 6 percent of its value, not 4. It also adds the school tax a home you live in does not pay. Its yearly bill is more than three times as high. Our guide to <a href="/invest/new-construction-rentals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">new construction as a rental</a> has the rest.</span></li><li><span class="c3-nc-ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span><span class="k">You want to be near the beach</span><span class="d">New houses are a small share of what is for sale near the ocean. Three of the <a href="#where" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">ten busiest new communities</a> are about 1 to 2 miles from it.</span></li></ul></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="where"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Where">Where are new homes being built around Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Mostly inland, in large planned communities between Conway and North Myrtle Beach. These ten recorded the most builder sales in Horry County in the 12 months to September 2026.</p><figure class="c3-nc-map" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.2rem;max-width:560px"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 440 430" role="img" aria-label="Map of Horry County with a dot for each house for sale. New houses, in orange, crowd around Conway, Longs, Loris and Aynor. Near the beach most dots are gray, older houses. Numbers 1 to 10 mark the communities where builders sold the most homes, most of them between Conway and North Myrtle Beach."><defs><clipPath id="c3-nc-frame"><rect width="440" height="430"/></clipPath><clipPath id="c3-nc-county"><path d="M288.7,337.3L273.1,348.3L264.4,356.2L241.2,379.7L208.9,414.7L162.0,424.1L160.0,426.1L159.5,424.3L126.7,424.8L120.3,423.9L120.2,417.5L121.3,411.2L120.4,402.9L118.3,403.1L117.5,407.8L115.7,408.5L111.6,404.1L109.8,402.4L110.2,399.0L109.6,395.2L107.4,394.3L106.7,391.4L107.1,389.9L104.9,388.4L107.3,386.3L104.5,382.2L105.7,381.4L108.2,384.4L109.7,379.6L107.7,380.7L105.8,377.6L103.7,372.9L101.6,376.0L96.7,376.2L95.6,373.7L96.7,368.1L95.0,363.4L93.4,360.8L89.1,358.1L83.6,355.4L85.2,353.2L84.5,351.6L78.4,349.2L76.5,346.3L76.6,343.7L77.9,340.9L74.5,335.2L72.6,333.6L72.2,332.2L68.5,329.4L67.6,327.8L65.4,326.2L65.4,325.3L66.5,323.5L65.9,321.9L64.7,320.9L61.8,320.6L60.6,318.0L58.3,317.6L58.4,314.7L57.8,312.6L57.5,311