oke-width="1.8"/><text x="150.3" y="342.4" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter,system-ui,sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">3</text><path d="M267.4 296.8L244.4 311.8" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="1.6"/><circle cx="267.4" cy="296.8" r="2.6" fill="#1c2028"/><circle cx="244.4" cy="311.8" r="9.5" fill="#1c2028" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="1.8"/><text x="244.4" y="316.4" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter,system-ui,sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">4</text><path d="M283.7 261.6L275.7 237.6" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="1.6"/><circle cx="283.7" cy="261.6" r="2.6" fill="#1c2028"/><circle cx="275.7" cy="237.6" r="9.5" fill="#1c2028" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="1.8"/><text x="275.7" y="242.2" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter,system-ui,sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">5</text><path d="M308.5 284.2L296.5 262.2" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="1.6"/><circle cx="308.5" cy="284.2" r="2.6" fill="#1c2028"/><circle cx="296.5" cy="262.2" r="9.5" fill="#1c2028" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="1.8"/><text x="296.5" y="266.8" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter,system-ui,sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">6</text><path d="M290.3 199.1L278.3 189.1" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="1.6"/><circle cx="290.3" cy="199.1" r="2.6" fill="#1c2028"/><circle cx="278.3" cy="189.1" r="9.5" fill="#1c2028" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="1.8"/><text x="278.3" y="193.7" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter,system-ui,sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">7</text><circle cx="170.4" cy="236.8" r="2.6" fill="#1c2028"/><circle cx="170.4" cy="236.8" r="9.5" fill="#1c2028" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="1.8"/><text x="170.4" y="241.4" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter,system-ui,sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">8</text><path d="M182.8 357.2L195.8 370.2" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="1.6"/><circle cx="182.8" cy="357.2" r="2.6" fill="#1c2028"/><circle cx="195.8" cy="370.2" r="9.5" fill="#1c2028" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="1.8"/><text x="195.8" y="374.8" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter,system-ui,sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">9</text><path d="M262.5 267.3L246.5 250.3" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="1.6"/><circle cx="262.5" cy="267.3" r="2.6" fill="#1c2028"/><circle cx="246.5" cy="250.3" r="9.5" fill="#1c2028" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="1.8"/><text x="246.5" y="254.9" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Inter,system-ui,sans-serif" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">10</text></g></svg><div class="c3-nc-key" style="margin:.6rem .2rem .1rem" aria-hidden="true"><span><i style="background:#c4783a;border-radius:50%;width:.8rem;height:.8rem"></i>New house for sale</span><span><i style="background:#5c6b78;border-radius:50%;width:.8rem;height:.8rem"></i>Any other house for sale</span><span><i style="background:#1c2028;border-radius:50%;width:.95rem;height:.95rem"></i>Community below</span></div><figcaption style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.55;margin:.8rem 0 0;padding:0">Each dot is a house for sale now. The numbers are the ten communities below. Map: Chapter3 Realty, from MLS listings, county records and Census map lines.</figcaption></figure><div class="c3-nc-cm" role="list" aria-label="The ten communities where builders sold the most homes from October 2025 to September 2026"><div role="listitem" class="c3-nc-card"><b class="n" aria-hidden="true">1</b><div class="bd"><span class="nm">Auberon Woods</span><p class="hs">D.R. Horton's page says the pool and pickleball courts are open, and a basketball court, a fitness room and sidewalks are on the way.</p><p class="ln">Conway address, outside city limits. Near Highway&nbsp;90, about 6&nbsp;miles from the ocean.</p><p class="ln">Built by D.R. Horton. Buyers paid a typical price of about $390,000.</p><a class="go" href="/homes/map/?type=house&amp;subdivision=Auberon+Woods">Homes for sale in Auberon Woods<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></div><div role="listitem" class="c3-nc-card"><b class="n" aria-hidden="true">2</b><div class="bd"><span class="nm">Grande Dunes North Village</span><span class="pl">County record: Grande Dunes North</span><p class="hs">A gated part of Grande Dunes with a staffed guardhouse. Ryan Homes' page says lawn care is included and residents have access to the Grande Dunes Ocean Club, the golf and the marina on the Intracoastal Waterway.</p><p class="ln">Longs address, inside North Myrtle Beach city limits. Near U.S.&nbsp;17, about 2&nbsp;miles from the ocean.</p><p class="ln">Built by NVR (Ryan Homes). Buyers paid a typical price of about $400,000.</p><a class="go" href="/homes/map/?type=house&amp;subdivision=Grande+Dunes&amp;city=Longs">Homes for sale in Grande Dunes North Village<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></div><div role="listitem" class="c3-nc-card"><b class="n" aria-hidden="true">3</b><div class="bd"><span class="nm">Arcadia</span><p class="hs">The only one of the ten where three builders sell, so you can compare their plans in one place.</p><p class="ln">Myrtle Beach address, outside city limits. Near the Carolina Bays Parkway, about 6&nbsp;miles from the ocean.</p><p class="ln">Built by Clayton Properties, Pulte and Lennar. Buyers paid a typical price of about $420,000.</p><a class="go" href="/homes/map/?type=house&amp;subdivision=Arcadia&amp;near=33.709%2C-79.0044&amp;miles=1.5">Homes for sale in Arcadia<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></div><div role="listitem" class="c3-nc-card"><b class="n" aria-hidden="true">4</b><div class="bd"><span class="nm">Waterside</span><span class="pl">County record: Waterside Neighborhood</span><p class="hs">Meritage's page lists a swimming pool, a cabana, a dog park, a tennis court, a bocce court, a community garden, a tot lot and a boat dock.</p><p class="ln">Longs address, inside North Myrtle Beach city limits. Near Highway&nbsp;22, about 2&nbsp;miles from the ocean.</p><p class="ln">Built by Meritage. Buyers paid a typical price of about $365,000.</p><a class="go" href="/homes/map/?type=house&amp;subdivision=Waterside&amp;city=Longs">Homes for sale in Waterside<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></div><div role="listitem" class="c3-nc-card"><b class="n" aria-hidden="true">5</b><div class="bd"><span class="nm">The Overlook</span><span class="pl">County record: Indigo Grove</span><p class="hs">With Kingston Oaks, also built by Lennar, it had the lowest typical price of the ten.</p><p class="ln">Longs address, outside city limits. Near Highway&nbsp;90, about 5&nbsp;miles from the ocean.</p><p class="ln">Built by Lennar. Buyers paid a typical price of about $245,000.</p><a class="go" href="/homes/map/?type=house&amp;subdivision=The+Overlook">Homes for sale in The Overlook<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></div><div role="listitem" class="c3-nc-card"><b class="n" aria-hidden="true">6</b><div class="bd"><span class="nm">Del Webb North Myrtle Beach</span><span class="pl">County record: Chestnut Greens</span><p class="hs">A 55+ community from Del Webb, Pulte's brand. Its page lists indoor and outdoor pools, an owner's clubhouse, a fitness center, sports courts and a lifestyle director.</p><p class="ln">North Myrtle Beach address, inside North Myrtle Beach city limits. Near U.S.&nbsp;17, about 1&nbsp;mile from the ocean.</p><p class="ln">Built by Pulte. Buyers paid a typical price of about $635,000.</p><a class="go" href="/homes/map/?type=house&amp;subdivision=Del+Webb&amp;city=North+Myrtle+Beach">Homes for sale in Del Webb North Myrtle Beach<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></div><div role="listitem" class="c3-nc-card"><b class="n" aria-hidden="true">7</b><div class="bd"><span class="nm">Cypress Ridge</span><p class="hs">Meritage builds here and at Waterside. Here, inland, buyers paid about $70,000 less for a typical house than at Waterside, near the beach.</p><p class="ln">Longs address, outside city limits. Near Highway&nbsp;9, about 11&nbsp;miles from the ocean.</p><p class="ln">Built by Meritage. Buyers paid a typical price of about $295,000.</p><a class="go" href="/homes/map/?type=house&amp;subdivision=Cypress+Ridge">Homes for sale in Cypress Ridge<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></div><div role="listitem" class="c3-nc-card"><b class="n" aria-hidden="true">8</b><div class="bd"><span class="nm">Kingston Oaks</span><p class="hs">Lennar's page lists a pool, a picnic area, a playground and a barbecue area as future amenities, and places the community near downtown Conway and Coastal Carolina University.</p><p class="ln">Conway address, inside Conway city limits. About 2&nbsp;miles from Highway&nbsp;22, about 15&nbsp;miles from the ocean.</p><p class="ln">Built by Lennar. Buyers paid a typical price of about $245,000.</p><a class="go" href="/homes/map/?type=house&amp;subdivision=Kingston+Oaks">Homes for sale in Kingston Oaks<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></div><div role="listitem" class="c3-nc-card"><b class="n" aria-hidden="true">9</b><div class="bd"><span class="nm">Crescent Cove</span><p class="hs">On the Intracoastal Waterway near Socastee. Pulte's page lists a day dock, a pool and a playground as coming soon, and a planned boat ramp.</p><p class="ln">Myrtle Beach address, outside city limits. Near Socastee Boulevard, about 4&nbsp;miles from the ocean.</p><p class="ln">Built by Pulte. Buyers paid a typical price of about $460,000.</p><a class="go" href="/homes/map/?type=house&amp;subdivision=Crescent+Cove">Homes for sale in Crescent Cove<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></div><div role="listitem" class="c3-nc-card"><b class="n" aria-hidden="true">10</b><div class="bd"><span class="nm">Eden Springs</span><p class="hs">D.R. Horton's page lists a pool, a pond and a community garden.</p><p class="ln">Longs address, outside city limits. Near Highway&nbsp;90, about 6&nbsp;miles from the ocean.</p><p class="ln">Built by D.R. Horton. Buyers paid a typical price of about $350,000.</p><a class="go" href="/homes/map/?type=house&amp;subdivision=Eden+Springs">Homes for sale in Eden Springs<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></div></div><p class="c3-nc-note">Builders and prices: county deeds for the same 12 months; the price is what buyers paid the builder. Ocean miles are straight lines. What each community has: the builder's own page.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Tour these communities with your own agent</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us the ones you like. We set up the visits and register with the builder as your agent.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Set up my builder tour</a></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">By town, new houses are more than half of the houses for sale in Loris, Longs, Aynor, Conway and Galivants Ferry addresses. Near the ocean they are a small share.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list [role=row]{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) auto;column-gap:.8rem;align-items:start}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .b{display:none}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .dot{display:none}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .f{display:block}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list [role=cell]{justify-content:flex-end}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact c3-gchart-list"><div role="table" aria-label="Share of houses for sale that are new, by town"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Share of houses for sale that are new, by town</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Town</span><span role="columnheader">share new</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Loris</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.64" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">64%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Longs</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.57" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">57%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Aynor</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.55" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">55%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Conway</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.55" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">55%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Galivants Ferry</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.52" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">52%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Little River</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.24" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">24%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Myrtle Beach</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.18" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">18%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">North Myrtle Beach</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.11" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">11%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Surfside Beach</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.08" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">8%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Murrells Inlet</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.04" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">4%</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Houses for sale in Horry County, grouped by the town in the address. Towns with 30 or more houses for sale.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our page on <a href="/invest/what-is-being-built/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">what is being built</a> covers the permits, the new roads and the hospitals.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Who builds new homes here?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Builders sold more than 1 in 4 homes recorded in Horry County in those 12 months. Five builders recorded about 7 in 10 of those sales.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Homes sold by builders in Horry County in the past year, by builder"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Homes sold by builders in Horry County in the past year, by builder</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Builder</span><span role="columnheader">sales recorded</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">D.R. Horton</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.943" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">1,417 sales</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Lennar</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.654" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">982 sales</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">NVR, parent of Ryan Homes</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.326" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">490 sales</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Pulte</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.255" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">383 sales</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Meritage</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.222" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">334 sales</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Every other builder</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">1,502 sales</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Sales recorded in the county's deed records, October 2025 to September 2026.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="cost"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Cost">What does a new house cost in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A typical new house for sale in Horry County is listed at about $370,000, with about 1,900 square feet on just under a quarter acre. Half are listed for more, half for less. That is an asking price; the tax example below uses what buyers paid.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="New houses for sale in Horry County, by asking price"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">New houses for sale in Horry County, by asking price</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Asking price</span><span role="columnheader">houses for sale</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">$300,000 or less</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.514" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">198 houses</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">$300,000 to $400,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">385 houses</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">$400,000 to $500,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.494" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">190 houses</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">$500,000 to $750,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.387" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">149 houses</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Over $750,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.218" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">84 houses</span></span></div></div></div></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most new houses come with an HOA fee. About 1 in 5 new houses for sale has none. For about 3 in 4, the fee is $100 a month or less, or there is none. Our guide to <a href="/buyers/no-hoa-homes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">homes with no HOA</a> lists the areas where most homes have none, and our guide to the <a href="/buyers/affordable-places-to-live/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">most affordable places to live</a> covers the lowest prices.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="tax-bill"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="What the price leaves out">What does the price of a new house leave out?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Five things: the full property tax, lot premiums, options and upgrades, HOA charges and closing costs. First the tax. A South Carolina <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c037.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">tax year looks back</a> to December 31 of the year before. A house finished after that date, or still unsold in the builder's hands, is usually not in that year's bill. Your first bill is often for the lot alone.</p><figure class="c3-nc-fig" role="group" aria-label="Homes builders sold in Horry County each month from October 2025 to September 2026, and how many the county still taxes as a lot. None sold in late 2025; most sold in 2026."><span class="c3-nc-cap">Homes builders sold each month, and how many the county still taxes as a lot</span><div class="c3-nc-key" aria-hidden="true"><span><i style="background:#c4783a"></i>Still taxed as a lot</span><span><i style="background:#5c6b78"></i>House value on the tax roll</span></div><div class="c3-nc-cols" aria-hidden="true"><span title="2025-10: 0 of 399"><i style="height:77.6%;background:#5c6b78"></i><i style="height:0.0%;background:#c4783a"></i></span><span title="2025-11: 0 of 405"><i style="height:78.8%;background:#5c6b78"></i><i style="height:0.0%;background:#c4783a"></i></span><span title="2025-12: 0 of 479"><i style="height:93.2%;background:#5c6b78"></i><i style="height:0.0%;background:#c4783a"></i></span><span title="2026-01: 115 of 353"><i style="height:46.3%;background:#5c6b78"></i><i style="height:22.4%;background:#c4783a"></i></span><span title="2026-02: 234 of 358"><i style="height:24.1%;background:#5c6b78"></i><i style="height:45.5%;background:#c4783a"></i></span><span title="2026-03: 294 of 404"><i style="height:21.4%;background:#5c6b78"></i><i style="height:57.2%;background:#c4783a"></i></span><span title="2026-04: 321 of 391"><i style="height:13.6%;background:#5c6b78"></i><i style="height:62.5%;background:#c4783a"></i></span><span title="2026-05: 405 of 466"><i style="height:11.9%;background:#5c6b78"></i><i style="height:78.8%;background:#c4783a"></i></span><span title="2026-06: 470 of 514"><i style="height:8.6%;background:#5c6b78"></i><i style="height:91.4%;background:#c4783a"></i></span><span title="2026-07: 421 of 462"><i style="height:8.0%;background:#5c6b78"></i><i style="height:81.9%;background:#c4783a"></i></span><span title="2026-08: 398 of 421"><i style="height:4.5%;background:#5c6b78"></i><i style="height:77.4%;background:#c4783a"></i></span><span title="2026-09: 435 of 456"><i style="height:4.1%;background:#5c6b78"></i><i style="height:84.6%;background:#c4783a"></i></span></div><div class="c3-nc-mo" aria-hidden="true"><span>O</span><span>N</span><span>D</span><span>J</span><span>F</span><span>M</span><span>A</span><span>M</span><span>J</span><span>J</span><span>A</span><span>S</span></div><div class="c3-nc-yr" aria-hidden="true"><span>2025</span><span>2026</span></div><figcaption style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.55;margin:.8rem 0 0;padding:0">For about 4 in 5 of the 2026 sales in the chart, the county record still shows the lot only, so the 2026 bill is on the lot. Every 2025 sale in the chart has its house value.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">When the county does value the house, it values it at about what you paid.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Take a typical 2026 builder sale that the county still taxes as a lot. It sold for $329,000, and the county values the lot at $80,000. A home you live in is taxed on 4 percent of its value once you apply; a second home or rental on 6 percent. Outside city limits, the yearly county tax looks like this:</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Kind of home</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Lot only</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Once valued</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Home you live in, 4 percent</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $290</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $1,210</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Second home or rental, 6 percent</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $960</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $3,970</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Inside a city, the city's own tax is added, so the bill is higher. Of the ten communities above, Grande Dunes North Village, Waterside and Del Webb North Myrtle Beach are inside North Myrtle Beach and Kingston Oaks is inside Conway. Our <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">property tax guide</a> has each city's rate.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Will the county bill you for the months before?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not for the months before the house stood on a December 31. The tax year looks back to that date, so the house tax starts with the next year's bill. If a house that was standing is left off the tax roll, the county may <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c039.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">bill the missed years</a>. It can go back no more than three years, and never to a year before the house was built.</p><ul class="c3-nc-check" role="list" aria-label="Two things to plan for with the tax bill on a new house"><li><span><strong>Apply for the 4 percent assessment.</strong> Without it, the county taxes your home like a second home, at 6 percent. Apply to the Horry County Assessor by January 15 of the year after you move in, before the <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/tax-payer-services/real-property-tax/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">first penalty date</a>. It <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c043.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">covers the whole year</a> if the house is the home you live in for any part of it. Overpaid tax can be refunded.</span></li><li><span><strong>Plan for a higher monthly payment later.</strong> If your lender collects the taxes with your loan, the tax part of the payment may go up once the house is valued. The lender's <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/rules-policy/regulations/1024/17/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">yearly escrow review</a> finds the difference.</span></li></ul><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Lot premiums, options and upgrades</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The price on the sign is for the base house. Pulte's pages for its communities here say the price <a href="https://www.pulte.com/homes/south-carolina/myrtle-beach/myrtle-beach/crescent-cove-211035" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">may not include</a> lot premiums, upgrades and options. A lot premium is an extra charge for a particular lot. Pulte's <a href="https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/822416/000082241626000007/phm-20251231.htm" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">annual report</a> names flooring, countertops, fixtures and appliances among its options.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Toll Brothers, which recorded 97 of the builder sales here, gives a national figure in its <a href="https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/794170/000079417025000112/tol-20251031.htm" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">annual report</a>. Its buyers' options and lot premiums came to about a quarter of the base price in its 2025 fiscal year. Its spec homes have less to add, it says.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Deposits</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">D.R. Horton, the builder with the most sales here, says in its <a href="https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/882184/000088218425000081/dhi-20250930.htm" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">annual report</a> that its contracts take an earnest money deposit, and more deposits if you pick options or upgrades. If a contract is cancelled, the deposit is kept or refunded under the contract's terms.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/owning-a-home/explore/find-the-right-home/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">deposit terms</a> matter before you sign. We go through them with you, along with the options you pick and what each one adds to the price.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">HOA charges and closing costs</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Closing costs come on top of the price. The federal Consumer Financial Protection Bureau (CFPB) says the buyer <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/ask-cfpb/what-fees-or-charges-are-paid-when-closing-on-a-mortgage-and-who-pays-them-en-1845/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">generally pays them</a>.</p><ul class="c3-nc-check" role="list" aria-label="Closing costs and HOA charges on a new house"><li><span><strong>What they include.</strong> The appraisal, title insurance, government taxes, and property taxes and homeowners insurance paid ahead.</span></li><li><span><strong>Help from the builder.</strong> Meritage, which recorded 334 sales here, says in its <a href="https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/833079/000083307926000010/mth-20251231.htm" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">annual report</a> that it may pay part of the closing costs for buyers who use its preferred lenders. A seller will usually want a higher price to cover a credit, the CFPB says.</span></li><li><span><strong>HOA charges.</strong> A new community's HOA can also charge at closing. Pulte's pages here list community association fees as a possible extra. Any HOA charge paid at closing is listed on your <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/rules-policy/regulations/1026/interp-38/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Closing Disclosure</a>. Ask the builder for the HOA's fees before you sign.</span></li></ul></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="your-agent"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Your own agent">Do you need a realtor for new construction?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">You can buy without one, but the salesperson in the model home works for the builder. Your own agent works for you. Nationwide, most of D.R. Horton's closings involve an independent real estate broker, its annual report says.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Since 2024, an agent asks you to sign a <a href="https://www.nar.realtor/the-facts/what-the-nar-settlement-means-for-home-buyers-and-sellers" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">written agreement</a> before you tour a home together. It states what the agent is paid, and that amount is fully negotiable. A builder, like any seller, can still offer to pay your agent. We confirm in writing what, if anything, you would pay before you tour.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Why does the first visit matter?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Each builder writes its own terms for paying a buyer's agent. Under D.R. Horton's <a href="https://www.drhorton.com/florida/southeast-florida/florida-city/palm-cay/qmis/1301-ne-4-avenue" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">terms on its Florida listings</a>, for example, the builder pays a buyer's agent only if the agent registers you on or before your first visit. You must also not have signed up on its website or talked with its sales agent first.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Tell us before you sign up online or walk into a model home, and we register with the builder as your agent from the start.</p><ul class="c3-nc-check" role="list" aria-label="What a Chapter3 agent does on a new build"><li><span><strong>Comes to your first visit.</strong> We register with the builder as your agent from the start.</span></li><li><span><strong>Reads the contract and the incentives.</strong> The contract is the builder's own, and we go through it with you before you sign.</span></li><li><span><strong>Prices the house against its neighbors.</strong> We compare it with the nearly new houses for sale within a mile.</span></li><li><span><strong>Works out the tax bill.</strong> You see the bill on the finished house before you sign.</span></li><li><span><strong>Arranges three inspections.</strong> Before the drywall, before closing and in month&nbsp;11.</span></li></ul></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="incentives"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Incentives and lenders">Can you negotiate with a builder, and should you use the builder's lender?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, you can negotiate. We see most builders here offer incentives to buyers with an FHA, VA or conventional loan. Incentives for investors, whose loans are based on the rent the home brings in, are rare.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Some promotions come with the builder's own lender. Lennar's <a href="https://www.lennar.com/new-homes/south-carolina/myrtle-beach/conway/kingston-oaks" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Kingston Oaks page</a> offers promotions when you finance through Lennar Mortgage, and nationwide, D.R. Horton's mortgage subsidiary financed 81 percent of the homes it closed in its 2025 fiscal year. You never <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/owning-a-home/explore/find-the-right-home/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">have to use the builder's lender</a>.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The way to judge the offer is <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/owning-a-home/loan-estimate/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">full Loan Estimates</a> from more than one lender, side by side. A Loan Estimate is the form that lists a loan's costs. Any lender can run that comparison for you, including our preferred lender.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="how-long"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="How long it takes">Spec home or to-be-built: how long does a new house take?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A spec home, one the builder starts before it has a buyer, is often finished and ready now. Of the new houses for sale in the MLS feed, almost half are finished and never lived in. The rest are still being built.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A house the builder has not started takes months. <a href="https://www.census.gov/construction/nrc/xls/avg_starttocomp_cust.xlsx" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">In the South</a>, a builder's house took about 5 and a half months from start to finish in the 2025 figures. A house a contractor builds on your own lot took about 9 months.</p><figure class="c3-nc-fig c3-nc-photo" style="max-width:760px"><img src="/images/2026-10-d/buyers-new-construction/new-street-being-built-myrtle-beach-2023-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-10-d/buyers-new-construction/new-street-being-built-myrtle-beach-2023-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-10-d/buyers-new-construction/new-street-being-built-myrtle-beach-2023-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 760px" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Aerial view of a new neighborhood with curving streets and ponds: finished houses with gray roofs, bare dirt lots between them, a white concrete slab and a house still in open wood framing, marked 1 to 4" style="display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:14px"><ol class="c3-nc-key c3-nc-num" aria-label="What the numbers mark"><li>A bare lot. The county taxes it as land until it values the house.</li><li>A new concrete slab, outlined, the first step of the house.</li><li>A house in open framing, before the drywall.</li><li>Finished houses.</li></ol><figcaption style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.55;margin:.8rem 0 0;padding:0">New streets in the City of Myrtle Beach from above. Photo: USDA Farm Service Agency, NAIP, public domain. Numbers by Chapter3 Realty.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="inspections"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Inspections">What inspections does a new house need?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Three of your own: before the drywall, before closing and before the first year of the warranty ends. Each comes at the last point a problem is easy to see, or still the builder's to fix. The county or city also inspects, for the building code. Your own inspector works for you.</p><figure class="c3-nc-draw" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.4rem;max-width:560px"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 640 330" role="img" aria-label="Drawing of a wall before the drywall goes up: wooden studs, an electrical cable running through them to an outlet box, and two water pipes running up between the studs."><rect width="640" height="330" rx="18" fill="#f3ede4"/><rect x="40" y="290" width="560" height="18" fill="#cfae7f" stroke="#b8925f" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="40" y="22" width="560" height="18" fill="#cfae7f" stroke="#b8925f" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="70" y="40" width="22" height="250" fill="#e2c49a" stroke="#b8925f" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="190" y="40" width="22" height="250" fill="#e2c49a" stroke="#b8925f" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="310" y="40" width="22" height="250" fill="#e2c49a" stroke="#b8925f" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="430" y="40" width="22" height="250" fill="#e2c49a" stroke="#b8925f" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="550" y="40" width="22" height="250" fill="#e2c49a" stroke="#b8925f" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M40 170 C120 168 160 172 214 170 S300 172 330 176" fill="none" stroke="#e0b100" stroke-width="7" stroke-linecap="round"/><rect x="330" y="160" width="34" height="46" rx="4" fill="#3d6fb5" stroke="#284d82" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M480 290 V60" stroke="#c0392b" stroke-width="9" stroke-linecap="round"/><path d="M504 290 V60" stroke="#2f6fb1" stroke-width="9" stroke-linecap="round"/><path d="M124 80L150 70" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="124" cy="80" r="4" fill="#1c2028"/><text x="156" y="78" text-anchor="start" font-family="Inter,system-ui,sans-serif" font-size="26" font-weight="600" fill="#1c2028" paint-order="stroke" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="6" stroke-linejoin="round">Framing</text><path d="M258 172L236 238" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="258" cy="172" r="4" fill="#1c2028"/><text x="230" y="246" text-anchor="end" font-family="Inter,system-ui,sans-serif" font-size="26" font-weight="600" fill="#1c2028" paint-order="stroke" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="6" stroke-linejoin="round">Wiring</text><path d="M492 120L400 112" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="492" cy="120" r="4" fill="#1c2028"/><text x="394" y="120" text-anchor="end" font-family="Inter,system-ui,sans-serif" font-size="26" font-weight="600" fill="#1c2028" paint-order="stroke" stroke="#fbf8f3" stroke-width="6" stroke-linejoin="round">Pipes</text></svg><figcaption style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.55;margin:.8rem 0 0;padding:0">Before the drywall goes up, the framing, the wiring and the pipes are open to see. Drawing: Chapter3 Realty.</figcaption></figure><ol class="c3-nc-steps" aria-label="The three inspections on a new house"><li><strong>Before the drywall goes up.</strong>The inspector sees the framing, the wiring and the pipes while the walls are open. Once the drywall is up, a problem inside a wall is hidden.</li><li><strong>Before closing.</strong>What is still wrong goes on a written list for the builder, while you can still ask for fixes before you close.</li><li><strong>In month&nbsp;11.</strong>Book it before the one-year part of the warranty ends. It finds what to report while the builder still pays for the fix. We see many builders here also send a maintenance person once in the first year to fix defects and touch up paint.</li></ol><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We set up all three, ask the builder for the warranty booklet, and keep the list of what each one finds until the builder has fixed it.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="warranty-law"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Warranty and the law">What can you do when something is wrong with a new house?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Report it to the builder in writing, under the warranty. D.R. Horton <a href="https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/882184/000088218425000081/dhi-20250930.htm" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">gives 1 year</a> on most of the house, 2 years on major mechanical systems and 10 years on major structure. Other builders differ, and the written warranty states the terms.</p><figure class="c3-nc-fig c3-nc-tl" role="group" aria-label="After closing: the largest builder's warranty is 1 year on most of the house, 2 years on major mechanical systems and 10 years on major structure. South Carolina's outer limit for most defect claims is 8 years after the house is finished."><span class="c3-nc-cap">After closing: the largest builder's warranty, and the state's outer limit</span><div class="r"><div class="l"><span>Most of the house</span><b>1 year</b></div><div class="trk"><i style="width:10%;background:#c4783a"></i></div></div><div class="r"><div class="l"><span>Major mechanical systems</span><b>2 years</b></div><div class="trk"><i style="width:20%;background:#c4783a"></i></div></div><div class="r"><div class="l"><span>Major structure</span><b>10 years</b></div><div class="trk"><i style="width:100%;background:#c4783a"></i></div></div><div class="r"><div class="l"><span>Outer limit for most defect claims</span><b>8 years</b></div><div class="trk"><u style="left:80%"></u></div></div><div class="c3-nc-ax" aria-hidden="true"><span style="left:0">Closing</span><span style="left:50%">5 years</span><span style="left:100%">10 years</span></div><figcaption style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.55;margin:.8rem 0 0;padding:0">Warranty: D.R. Horton's, from its annual report. Law: the 8 years run from when the house is substantially complete.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The warranty says what the builder will fix. The state law says how long you have to sue. Most lawsuits over defects must be filed within 8 years of the house being finished. Inside that, most claims <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t15c003.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">must be filed within three years</a>.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If the builder will not fix it, under South Carolina's <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t40c059.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">defect law</a> you send the builder written notice, and the builder may inspect and offer a repair before you can sue. We keep track of your warranty deadlines after closing.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="new-construction-questions"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">New construction questions</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can I find a new house in Myrtle Beach under $300,000?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. About 1 in 5 new houses for sale in Horry County is listed at $300,000 or less. Of the ten communities where builders sold the most, The Overlook (Indigo Grove), Kingston Oaks and Cypress Ridge had typical sale prices under $300,000.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Are there new townhomes in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. 108 new townhouses are for sale in Horry County, at a typical list price of about $275,000 for about 1,580 square feet.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How does the county know a new house is being built?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">From the building permit. South Carolina law has every county require a permit for new construction. The county must send the assessor a copy of each building permit within 10 days, so the assessor knows a house is being built.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Does a home builder in South Carolina need a license?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. A residential builder needs a state license for any job over $5,000, issued by the Residential Builders Commission. A complaint against a builder goes to the Commission in writing and sworn.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/search/SearchTypeDocType" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">County deeds</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycounty.org/parcelapp/rest/services/HorryCountyGISApp/MapServer" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">County GIS</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycounty.org/parcelapp/rest/services/HorryCountyGISApp/MapServer/19" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Flood zones</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kufln4qp/tax-levy-2026_2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">2026 tax levy</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c043.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 12-43</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t38c073.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 38-73</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t40c059.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 40-59</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t15c003.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 15-3</a>, <a href="https://llr.sc.gov/res/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC builders board</a>, <a href="https://www.census.gov/construction/nrc/xls/avg_starttocomp_cust.xlsx" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census</a>, <a href="https://www.nar.realtor/the-facts/what-the-nar-settlement-means-for-home-buyers-and-sellers" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NAR</a>, <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/rules-policy/regulations/1024/17/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">12 CFR 1024.17</a>, <a href="https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/882184/000088218425000081/dhi-20250930.htm" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">D.R. Horton 10-K</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t06c009.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 6-9</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c039.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 12-39</a>, <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/owning-a-home/explore/find-the-right-home/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CFPB</a>, <a href="https://www.lennar.com/new-homes/south-carolina/myrtle-beach/conway/kingston-oaks" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Lennar</a>, <a href="https://www.drhorton.com/florida/southeast-florida/florida-city/palm-cay/qmis/1301-ne-4-avenue" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">D.R. Horton terms</a>, <a href="https://www.pulte.com/homes/south-carolina/myrtle-beach/myrtle-beach/crescent-cove-211035" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pulte</a>, <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/rules-policy/regulations/1026/interp-38/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Reg Z</a>. Homes for sale: our count of MLS listings, in aggregate. Sales: county deeds, October 2025 to September 2026. Not legal or tax advice.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">New streets in the City of Myrtle Beach from above. Photo: USDA Farm Service Agency, NAIP, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty exported this view from the NAIP image service, added four numbered markers and an outline round the slab, cut it to the middle of the street and resized it.</div></div></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Tour new builds with your own agent</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.75);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:1.6rem">Tell us the communities you like. We price each house against the nearly new houses around it, work out its tax bill once it is valued, and set up the inspections.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Set up my builder tour</a></div></section></main>
